# Git push to REM

Remote: `https://github.com/SjPn/REM.git` (`origin`).

After finishing a meaningful code/UI/docs change in this project:

1. Commit the relevant files (never `.env`, `*.db`, secrets, `.venv`).
2. Push to `origin` on the current branch (usually `main`) without waiting for the user to ask.
3. Prefer Windows Credential Manager / stored GitHub credentials (`git:https://github.com`); do not ask the user to re-authenticate if credentials already exist.
4. After push, briefly confirm with the commit message and repo URL.

Do not force-push to `main` unless the user explicitly requests it.
